  "generated_answer": "## Learning Objectives for Money in Primary 4 Mathematics\n\nBased on the retrieved curriculum evidence, the learning objectives related to money in Primary 4 Mathematics are as follows:\n\n### Unit: Everyday Arithmetic (C4-U17)\n- **C4U17-LO01** \u2014 Add money up to Le 5,000, Le10,000, Le 20,000 and Le 50,000\n- **C4U17-LO02** \u2014 Subtract money up to Le 5,000, Le10,000, Le 20,000 and Le 50,000.\n\n### Unit: Everyday Arithmetic Money (C4-U18)\n- **C4U18-LO01** \u2014 Order operations using BODMAS.\n- **C4U18-LO02** \u2014 Solve word problems involving the 4 operations and money.\n- **C4U18-LO03** \u2014 Estimate strategies to check answers for reasonableness\n- **C4U18-LO04** \u2014 Inverse operations to check answers for reasonableness.\n\nThese objectives cover addition and subtraction of money amounts, solving word problems that combine money with the four operations, and using estimation and inverse operations to verify answers.",
